<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY - see Disposition__c.field-meta.xml
        in this folder for why a comment above the root breaks `sf` deploy.

        🔴 A SNAPSHOT, NOT A REDUNDANCY. Outgoing_Broker__c is deleteConstraint SetNull, and
        scripts/seed-broker-contacts.apex mass-deletes every Contact on the Contact.Broker
        record type. (⚠ CORRECTED 2026-08-20 — this read "every Contact flagged Is_Broker__c
        (`delete [SELECT Id FROM Contact WHERE Is_Broker__c = true]`)". Both halves are stale:
        the inline delete was hoisted into a guarded six-step structure, and the broker
        definition moved to the record type. 🔴 THE MOVE MADE THIS HAZARD REAL RATHER THAN
        THEORETICAL: measured on usman-dpeg, the old predicate matched ZERO rows org-wide, so
        that delete was a guaranteed no-op; the new one matches ~19 live brokers.) Re-running
        that script
        against an org holding BOV_Broker_Change__c rows NULLS Outgoing_Broker__c on every row
        pointing at a deleted broker, silently and with no error. A history row whose broker
        column reads blank at that point is not history - it is exactly the corruption-that-
        reads-as-health BOV_Submission__c.Broker_Firm__c's own comment describes for the same
        seed script. This Text field is stamped by BovSubmissionService.replaceSelectedBroker
        (developer-owned, D4.3) at write time from the Contact chosen in Outgoing_Broker__c, and
        it is NOT retired or superseded by that lookup - it is the field that survives the
        lookup going blank.

        Length 255, unrequired, unindexed - a plain snapshot, matching Broker_Firm__c's own shape
        on BOV_Submission__c (Text 255, not unique, not an external Id).
    -->
    <fullName>Outgoing_Broker_Firm__c</fullName>
    <externalId>false</externalId>
    <description>Snapshot of the outgoing broker's firm at the time of this change. Stamped from Outgoing_Broker__c; survives that Contact later being deleted (Outgoing_Broker__c is deleteConstraint SetNull and scripts/seed-broker-contacts.apex mass-deletes broker Contacts).</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Filled in automatically from the outgoing broker's Contact record. Do not type into it.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Outgoing Broker Firm</label>
    <length>255</length>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Text</type>
    <unique>false</unique>
</CustomField>
